cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or analysis workflow, please cite the archived software release and the associated manuscript."
title: "Post-export RNA kinetics: reproducibility code for compartment-resolved kinetic inference"
type: software
version: "manuscript-revision-v1.0"
license: "MIT"

authors:
  - family-names: "Faretra"
    given-names: "L."
  - family-names: "Napolitano"
    given-names: "F."
  - family-names: "Pancione"
    given-names: "M."
  - family-names: "Cerulo"
    given-names: "L."

repository-code: "https://github.com/bioinformatics-sannio/postexport-kinetics"

abstract: >-
  Reproducibility code and analysis workflows accompanying the revised
  Bioinformatics manuscript BIOINF-2026-0699. The repository implements
  compartment-resolved RNA kinetic modeling, constrained nested-model
  comparison, replicate-level generative bootstrap inference, corrected
  synthetic benchmarking, pseudo-shutoff and model-misspecification analyses,
  practical-identifiability analyses, comparator analyses, and final real-data
  workflows. The post-export conversion parameter is interpreted
  phenomenologically and does not by itself identify a specific molecular
  mechanism.

keywords:
  - RNA kinetics
  - post-export RNA processing
  - post-export conversion
  - compartment-resolved RNA
  - transcriptomics
  - kinetic modeling
  - bootstrap inference
  - retained introns
  - reproducible research
